[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
RustFS is configured through rc.conf(5) variables, see
%%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/rustfs, and optionally RUSTFS_* environment
variables in %%PREFIX%%/etc/rustfs.env.

Change the default credentials immediately: set unique access key and
secret key values. Do not use the well-known rustfsadmin value for either
credential. Use a unique access key and a strong, random secret (e.g.
openssl rand -base64 24):

  sysrc rustfs_access_key="your-access-key"
  sysrc rustfs_secret_key="your-secret-key"

Restart the service with "service rustfs restart" after changing them.

In Single Node Single Disk (SNSD) mode, one server stores all data on a
single data disk. A single drive offers no redundancy. If the drive fails,
data is lost. This is the default, with the data in %%DBDIR%%.

In Single Node Multiple Disk (SNMD) mode, one server shards data across
multiple data disks. Mount each disk separately and list the mount points
in rustfs_volumes. Local erasure endpoints must use distinct physical disks.

Open the Console: in a browser, go to http://<server-ip>:9001.
EOM
}
]
